        "original_id": "8ef8e488-f50a-5e2e-ba0c-4b05cddc2a87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Tashlin, Craig Serling\n- Works: Brother Brat, Jam\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Topics: animation, film directing, screenwriting, television editing\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Tashlin, born Francis Fredrick von Taschlein on February 19, 1913, was an American animator, screenwriter, and film director.\n- Brother Brat is a 1944 Warner Bros. Looney Tunes theatrical cartoon short starring Porky Pig and directed by Frank Tashlin.\n- Craig Serling is an American film director, film producer, screenwriter, and television editor.\n- Craig Serling is known for multiple Primetime Emmy nominations for Outstanding Picture Editing for Non-Fiction Programming.\n- Craig Serling made his directorial feature film debut in 2006 with Jam.\n- Frank Tashlin died on May 5, 1972.",
